{"67ccf94b2a": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "If you think your skills, experience and aspirations make you a good match for this position, we encourage you to apply."}, {"h": "ABOUT THE ROLE", "t": "Under the direction of a licensed engineer and designated project leadership, the successful candidate will be responsible for analysis and design of structural systems/components in steel, concrete and masonry and an integral part of design teams.\nClick here to learn more about our Engineering practice"}, {"h": "HERE'S WHAT YOU'LL DO", "t": "Independently perform structural engineering tasks on multiple projects.\nInterface effectively with members of the design team to coordinate structural systems with overall building design.\nPerform design calculations. Use relevant engineering software to design and document structural engineering systems.\nIdentify and apply structural code knowledge to structural engineering work. Design complete structural system within established design parameters.\nUse Revit to develop BIM models for producing contract documents.\nPerform complex design calculations and limited custom detailing.\nIndependently check shop drawings and calculations.\nReview and edit design specifications.\nInterface effectively with clients.\nMay attend and participate in construction meetings.\nPerform field observations during construction phase requiring a physical walk through of the site. Observations may be done independently.\nMay guide technicians and less experienced staff in execution of contract documents.\nMay assist in defining project budget and scope.\nMust be willing to perform overtime work and travel."}, {"h": "Minimum 4 years of related experience required.", "t": "Current PE and/or SE in the United States required."}, {"h": "LEED AP is preferred.", "t": "Experience with concrete and steel required.\nKnowledge of IBC and other national standard codes.\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills.\nAble to effectively handle multiple projects.\nExperience in computer applications for engineering design programs (i.e. Revit, RAM, RISA) required.\nThe salary range for this position to be filled in the Buffalo, NY office is $71,502 to $89,352 annually. This salary range is the range we believe is the anticipated range of possible base compensation at the timing of the posting. We may ultimately pay more or less than the anticipated salary range for the position.\n\nBased on the position status, employees may be eligible for discretionary bonuses and a full benefit package including medical, dental and vision coverage and flexible spending account options and voluntary insurances. We have paid time off, flex-time schedules, remote work options and a 401k plan and employee perk programs.\n\nFor a general overview of our benefits, please visit our careers page at https://www.cannondesign.com/careers/benefits . Actual compensation may vary from posting based on geographic location, work experience, education and/or skill level."}, {"h": "ABOUT OUR FIRM", "t": "CannonDesign is a design practice where strategy, experience, architecture, engineering, and social impact converge. We don’t just dream up solutions — we create and bring them to life in ways to solve some of the biggest challenges facing our clients and the society.\n\nAt the heart of everything we do is Living-Centered Design, a bold commitment to using our talents to not just improve the world but to truly reshape it for the better. It’s more than a philosophy — it’s who we are, and it drives us to make a meaningful, lasting difference every day."}, {"h": "ABOUT WORKING HERE", "t": "We are relentless in our pursuit of client adoration (not simply satisfaction). Consistent delivery of the best service is what we are about.\nWe are committed to ensuring our practice provides equal opportunities for all employees, as we strive to connect with communities around us and focus on the future of design. We support equity, diversity, and inclusion efforts that benefit all employees through the leadership of our DEI Council, our Employee Resource Groups which are open to everyone, and other community initiatives.\nWe’re about communication and transparency here. If you want to talk to someone about an idea you have, or a challenge that needs addressing, we’re ready for you.\nPlease note that candidates can only apply to our positions on our company Careers site. It's not uncommon for scammers to create positions that look legitimate on other sites; never enter your information or apply for CannonDesign positions on any platform. Should an issue arise that you feel we should be aware of, please contact us. Please provide your resume and portfolio when applying.\nAs a condition of employment, all employees are expected to complete mandatory training, including compliance training, within required timeframes and adhere to our internal policies and our Code of Conduct.\nCannonDesign is an Equal Opportunity Employer. CannonDesign is committed to maintaining a work environment that is free from any and all forms of unlawful discrimination and harassment.\n\nIt is therefore the firm’s policy to prohibit discrimination and harassment against any applicant, CannonDesign employee, vendor, contractor, or client on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, pregnancy, veteran status, genetic information, citizenship status, or any other basis prohibited by applicable law.\n\nIt is also CannonDesign’s policy to prohibit any and all forms of retaliation against any individual who has complained of harassing or discriminatory conduct, or participated in a firm or agency investigation into such complaints."}], "k": ["bim", "building-codes", "cad-drafting", "detailing", "etabs", "leed", "revit"]}, "5cf6946f72": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "DLR Group is an integrated design firm with a promise to elevate the human experience through design. This fuels the work we do around the world and inspires our mission to improve the lives of our clients, our communities, and our planet. If this sparks your interest, you’re in the right place.\nWe have an opening for a Senior Structural Engineer. This role can be based in the following cities:\nLocation: Denver, CO, Phoenix, AZ, and Las Vegas, NV"}, {"h": "Position Summary", "t": "As a Senior Structural Engineer, you will be responsible for leading design of structural systems for buildings across a variety of sectors including K-12, Higher Education, Justice & Civic, Cultural and Performing Arts, and Mixed Use.\n\nYou will lead a team of junior staff to produce high-quality construction documents using Revit and manage project schedules to meet deliverable requirements. As part of the integrated design team, you will collaborate closely with other disciplines to produce highly integrated building designs.\n\nThis role will work directly with the regional discipline leader to assist in developing work plans, project schedules, budgets, and proposals for both internal teams and external clients."}, {"h": "The successful candidate will", "t": "Strive for excellence in developing structural solutions from concept through construction.\nBe a decision-maker in developing system layouts, narratives, calculations and engineering reports.\nWelcome deep collaboration with architects, other engineers, and clients as part of our integrated design process.\nLearn and adapt to variations in building codes and construction practices while working on projects around the US.\nProduce construction documents using Revit.\nAssist contractors by reviewing shop drawings, RFIs and participating in O/A/C meetings.\nPass along knowledge by mentoring entry-level staff.\nPromote workflow and technical standards best-practices for our diverse multi-office practice.\nContribute to managing the operations, execution, and expectations for the Structural Engineering Discipline in Colorado.\nSupport business development initiatives by assisting the RFP process, participating in project interviews, and actively engaging in community and/or industry specific organization that will build the DLR Group brand."}, {"h": "Required Qualifications", "t": "Bachelor's degree in Civil/Structural/Architectural Engineering; Master’s degree preferred.\n10+ years of building related structural engineering experience, including the design of concrete, masonry, steel and wood/timber; gravity and lateral systems.\nLicensed Professional Engineer (PE) in the State of California, Licensed Structural Engineer (SE) preferred\nPrior experience leading teams of engineers on projects.\nWorking knowledge of current structural software (ETABS, SAP, SAFE, RAM, ADAPT, RISA, Enercalc).\nExperience with BIM including Autodesk Revit workflow.\nGoal oriented with strong skills in problem solving, creativity, and attention to detail.\nUnderstanding of commercial building materials, systems, and assemblies.\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills.\nPassion for sustainable building design and SE2050 commitment.\nExperience with directing and coordinating project activities of junior staff.\nOur comprehensive Benefits at DLR Group include medical, dental, vision, disability, wellness programs, flex spending, paid holidays, and paid time off. We also offer a 401(k) plan, employee stock ownership, and bonus opportunities. Compensation considerations are based on location, experience, and skills. The suggested pay range for this position is:"}, {"h": "$110,000 — $144,000 USD", "t": "DLR Group is an integrated design firm delivering architecture, engineering, interiors, planning, and building optimization for new builds, renovations, and adaptive reuse projects.\nWe are 100% employee-owned: every employee is literally invested in our clients’ success. At the core of our firm are interdisciplinary teams engaged in every step of project lifecycles.\n\nOur teams champion true collaboration, open information sharing, shared risk and reward, value-based decision making, and proficient use of technology to deliver exceptional design. We are pursuing the goals of the 2030 Challenge, the ME2040, and the SE2050, and are an initial signatory of the China Accord and the AIA 2030 Commitment.\nThrough our values – commitment, creativity, environmental stewardship, fun, integrity, ownership, sharing, teamwork – we elevate the human experience through design, together.\nDLR Group follows a four-day in-office work model, with employees having the flexibility to work somewhere other than the office on Fridays.\nWe are proud to be an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/M/F/Veteran/Disabled employer."}], "k": ["bim", "building-codes", "business-development", "cad-drafting", "construction-administration", "construction-documents", "etabs", "procurement", "project-management", "revit", "sap", "training"]}, "aa0e15bf63": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "DLR Group is an integrated design firm with a promise to elevate the human experience through design. This fuels the work we do around the world and inspires our mission to improve the lives of our clients, our communities, and our planet. If this sparks your interest, you’re in the right place.\nThe Engineering team has an opening for a Structural Engineer."}, {"h": "Locations", "t": "Sacramento, CA\nSan Diego, CA"}, {"h": "Position Summary", "t": "As a Structural Engineer at DLR Group you will be responsible for participating in the design process of structural building systems from schematics through construction administration preparing detailed structural engineering drawings and performing design calculations. As part of our integrated design teams you will create buildings that elevate the human experience through design."}, {"h": "The successful candidate will", "t": "Strive for excellence in developing structural solutions from concept through construction.\nBe a decision-maker in developing system layouts, narratives, calculations and engineering reports.\nWelcome deep collaboration with architects, other engineers, and clients as part of our integrated design process.\nLearn and adapt to variations in building codes and construction practices while working on projects around the US.\nProduce construction documents using Revit.\nAssist contractors by reviewing shop drawings, RFIs and participating in O/A/C meetings.\nPass along knowledge by mentoring entry-level staff.\nPromote workflow and technical standards best-practices for our diverse multi-office practice."}, {"h": "Required Qualifications", "t": "Bachelor's degree in Civil/Structural/Architectural Engineering; Master’s degree preferred.\n5+ years of building related structural engineering experience, including the design of concrete, masonry, steel and wood/timber; gravity and lateral systems.\nLicensed Professional Engineer (PE), Licensed Structural Engineer (SE) preferred\nWorking knowledge of current structural software (ETABS, SAP, SAFE, RAM, ADAPT, RISA, Enercalc).\nExperience with BIM including Autodesk Revit workflow.\nGoal oriented with strong skills in problem solving, creativity, and attention to detail.\nUnderstanding of commercial building materials, systems, and assemblies.\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills.\nPassion for sustainable building design and SE2050 commitment."}, {"h": "Preferred Qualifications", "t": "Master’s Degree in Civil/Structural or Architectural/Structural Engineering.\nLicensed Professional Engineer (PE) in the State of California.\nExperience with BIM (e.g. Autodesk Revit Structural) workflow.\nExperience and interest in sustainable building design.\nExperience with design and construction of projects under DSA jurisdiction.\nOur comprehensive Benefits at DLR Group include medical, dental, vision, disability, wellness programs, flex spending, paid holidays, and paid time off. We also offer a 401(k) plan, employee stock ownership, and bonus opportunities. Compensation considerations are based on location, experience, and skills. The suggested pay range for this position is:"}, {"h": "$93,170 — $135,000 USD", "t": "DLR Group is an integrated design firm delivering architecture, engineering, interiors, planning, and building optimization for new builds, renovations, and adaptive reuse projects.\nWe are 100% employee-owned: every employee is literally invested in our clients’ success. At the core of our firm are interdisciplinary teams engaged in every step of project lifecycles.\n\nOur teams champion true collaboration, open information sharing, shared risk and reward, value-based decision making, and proficient use of technology to deliver exceptional design. We are pursuing the goals of the 2030 Challenge, the ME2040, and the SE2050, and are an initial signatory of the China Accord and the AIA 2030 Commitment.\nThrough our values – commitment, creativity, environmental stewardship, fun, integrity, ownership, sharing, teamwork – we elevate the human experience through design, together.\nDLR Group follows a four-day in-office work model, with employees having the flexibility to work somewhere other than the office on Fridays.\nWe are proud to be an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/M/F/Veteran/Disabled employer."}], "k": ["bim", "blueprint-reading", "building-codes", "cad-drafting", "construction-administration", "construction-documents", "etabs", "revit", "sap", "training"]}, "6064d3b23b": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\n\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\n\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\n\nJob Description\n\nAs an Assistant Engineer on the Rail Structures team at Olsson, you will support a variety of routine engineering tasks that enhance your technical knowledge and familiarity with industry practices, tools, and team collaboration. This entry-level role contributes to the development of purposeful, high-quality design solutions that address real-world engineering challenges, particularly in the railroad sector."}, {"h": "Primary duties and responsibilities", "t": "· Assist with project design elements using standard techniques and established methods.\n\n· Perform entry-level plan production with clearly defined instructions.\n\n· Gain experience working within design and modeling software.\n\n· Support senior staff with project schedules and technical engineering calculations.\n\n· Contribute to limited portions of broader projects under direct supervision.\n\n· Gather and prepare research for technical reports.\n\n· Provide mentoring to student interns by answering questions and guiding routine assignments.\n\n· Travel and work in various terrain and weather conditions at project sites in different construction stages."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "· Working collaboratively with others.\n\n· Having ownership in the work you do.\n\n· Using your talents to positively affect communities."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "· Bachelor’s degree in civil or structural engineering\n\n· Must possess or obtain Engineer Intern certificate (EI)\n\n· Experience in MicroStation, Risa 3D analysis, and Bluebeam Revu preferred\n\n· Strong communication skills\n\n· Strong problem-solving skills with keen attention to detail\n\n· Ability to contribute and work well on a team"}, {"h": "Expectations", "t": "· Adept in verbal and written communication\n\n· Solid interpersonal, problem-solving, and decision-making skills\n\n· Ability to diligently research applicable requirements and regulations\n\n· Advanced mathematical and analytical abilities\n\n· Working knowledge (or ability to become proficient) in applicable technologies\n\n· Understands their role in quality management\n\n· Develops an understanding of how the firm operates as a consulting business and how this role contributes to its success\n\n· Holds a valid driver’s license and maintains a good driving history\n\n· Willingness to work a flexible schedule\n\n· Represents Olsson in a professional manner at all times"}, {"h": "#LI-AF1", "t": "Actual compensation will vary based on factors such as experience, qualifications, geographic location, skills, education, and internal equity."}, {"h": "$79,000 — $104,000 USD", "t": "Additional Information\n\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "· Receive a competitive 401(k) match\n\n· Be empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\n\n· Have the possibility for flexible work arrangements\n\n· Engage in work that has a positive impact on communities\n\n· Participate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\n\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\n\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\n\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\n\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["bluebeam", "etabs", "microstation", "project-management", "training"]}, "3c36904eaa": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nWe are seeking an Associate Structural Engineer to join our Federal Engineering and Design Team. In this role, you will assist with structural design efforts for federal projects, including building frameworks, foundations, and structural systems.\n\nYou’ll collaborate closely with experienced engineers and designers, gaining exposure to federal standards such as UFC, DoD, and VA requirements, while strengthening your skills in structural analysis and modeling software.\n\nThis position offers hands-on experience and the opportunity to contribute to impactful projects within Olsson’s federal portfolio."}, {"h": "Key responsibilities", "t": "Provides structural design elements for federal engineering projects using fundamental knowledge of structural principles, standard techniques, and established methods for small to mid-sized projects.\nPerforms basic structural plan production and receives instructions for necessary tasks, including drafting and detailing structural components.\nDevelops and apply knowledge and experience working within structural design and modeling software, such as Revit, Risa, and other structural analysis tools.\nAssist with project schedules, engineering calculations, and preparation of construction documents.\nCoordinates with experienced structural engineers and designers on non-routine techniques and procedures to ensure compliance with codes and standards.\nGather research, recommend solutions, and create drafts of technical reports.\nMentor student interns by providing opportunities for developing basic structural engineering skills and knowledge.\nMay travel and work in various terrains and weather conditions at project sites in different stages of construction."}, {"h": "Why join us", "t": "Contribute to projects that serve national interests and make a difference in communities.\nEnjoy flexible work arrangements, including remote options, to support your work-life balance.\nThrive in a supportive culture that values professional development and teamwork."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities."}, {"h": "Preferred qualifications", "t": "We’re looking for candidates who bring both technical expertise and leadership potential:\nA minimum of one year of engineering experience.\nBachelor’s degree in civil or architectural engineering or a related engineering field.\nPossesses Engineer-In-Training (EIT) certification.\nStrong communication skills.\nAbility to contribute and work well with a team.\nSolid interpersonal, problem-solving, and decision-making skills.\nDemonstrates the ability to diligently research applicable structural codes, standards, and regulations.\nKnowledge in structural engineering technologies, such as Revit and structural analysis softwares.\nWillingness to travel and work in field conditions as needed.\nSolid interpersonal, problem-solving, and decision-making skills."}, {"h": "#LI-DNP", "t": "Additional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["construction-documents", "detailing", "etabs", "fea", "project-management", "revit", "structural-analysis"]}, "7409584137": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\n\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\n\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\n\nJob Description\n\nAs an Assistant Engineer on the Rail Structures team at Olsson, you will support a variety of routine engineering tasks that enhance your technical knowledge and familiarity with industry practices, tools, and team collaboration. This entry-level role contributes to the development of purposeful, high-quality design solutions that address real-world engineering challenges, particularly in the railroad sector."}, {"h": "Primary duties and responsibilities", "t": "· Assist with project design elements using standard techniques and established methods.\n\n· Perform entry-level plan production with clearly defined instructions.\n\n· Gain experience working within design and modeling software.\n\n· Support senior staff with project schedules and technical engineering calculations.\n\n· Contribute to limited portions of broader projects under direct supervision.\n\n· Gather and prepare research for technical reports.\n\n· Provide mentoring to student interns by answering questions and guiding routine assignments.\n\n· Travel and work in various terrain and weather conditions at project sites in different construction stages."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "· Working collaboratively with others.\n\n· Having ownership in the work you do.\n\n· Using your talents to positively affect communities."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "· Bachelor’s degree in civil or structural engineering\n\n· Must possess or obtain Engineer Intern certificate (EI)\n\n· Experience in MicroStation, Risa 3D analysis, and Bluebeam Revu preferred\n\n· Strong communication skills\n\n· Strong problem-solving skills with keen attention to detail\n\n· Ability to contribute and work well on a team"}, {"h": "Expectations", "t": "· Adept in verbal and written communication\n\n· Solid interpersonal, problem-solving, and decision-making skills\n\n· Ability to diligently research applicable requirements and regulations\n\n· Advanced mathematical and analytical abilities\n\n· Working knowledge (or ability to become proficient) in applicable technologies\n\n· Understands their role in quality management\n\n· Develops an understanding of how the firm operates as a consulting business and how this role contributes to its success\n\n· Holds a valid driver’s license and maintains a good driving history\n\n· Willingness to work a flexible schedule\n\n· Represents Olsson in a professional manner at all times"}, {"h": "#LI-AF1", "t": "Additional Information\n\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "· Receive a competitive 401(k) match\n\n· Be empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\n\n· Have the possibility for flexible work arrangements\n\n· Engage in work that has a positive impact on communities\n\n· Participate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\n\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\n\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\n\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\n\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["bluebeam", "etabs", "microstation", "project-management", "training"]}, "a1b58a01de": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nImagine being part of a team that supports the backbone of the electric grid. As a Structural Engineer – Substation, you will play a critical role in the planning, design, and delivery of substation infrastructure across Olsson’s Transmission and Substation team.\nIn this role, you will lead the structural design of substation foundations, steel structures, and equipment supports, contributing to projects that strengthen and modernize power delivery systems. You will collaborate closely with electrical engineers, designers, and project managers throughout all phases of project delivery.\nThis position is ideal for a structural engineer who enjoys technically challenging work, mentoring others, and contributing meaningfully to essential infrastructure projects."}, {"h": "Key Responsibilities", "t": "Structural Design & Analysis: Perform and lead structural design for substation facilities, including foundations, steel structures, equipment supports, and miscellaneous structural components.\nProject Delivery: Support projects through all phases including conceptual design, detailed engineering, permitting support, and construction administration.\nCoordination & Collaboration: Work closely with electrical engineers, designers, and other disciplines to ensure coordinated, constructible designs.\nTechnical Leadership: Provide technical guidance and review of designs prepared by junior engineers and designers.\nClient & Field Interaction: Participate in client meetings, respond to contractor RFIs, and provide construction support as needed, including limited travel to project sites."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "Bachelor’s degree in Structural Engineering or Civil Engineering (structural emphasis).\n6+ years of progressive structural engineering experience, preferably including substation or industrial facilities.\nExperience designing concrete foundations and structural steel systems.\nWorking knowledge of relevant codes and standards (ACI, AISC, IBC, ASCE).\nStrong communication, organizational, and problem‑solving skills.\nProfessional Engineer (PE) licensure preferred or ability to obtain within a reasonable timeframe."}, {"h": "#LI-DD1", "t": "Additional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["building-codes", "construction-administration", "project-management", "steel-design", "structural-analysis", "training"]}, "fe74d07bdc": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nOlsson's Facilities Engineering and Design Team is at the forefront of engineering innovation, providing comprehensive services for large commercial developments, healthcare facilities, laboratories, educational institutions, data centers, and military installations.\n\nOur expertise includes engineering analysis, design services, and professional consulting, ensuring top-tier quality and world class installations. We also provide building inspection and forensic investigation services.\n\nAs a member of this team, you will contribute to diverse, high-impact projects, delivering engineering solutions that make a tangible difference in communities and industries.\nThe Lead Engineer role oversees high-level project design and manages the overall design tasks within the structural group. As a Lead Engineer, you will make influential recommendations and decisions regarding advanced engineering activities and specialized client-type standards and have full technical responsibility of design assignments. This role manages the delivery of advanced project designs that provide purposeful, high-quality solutions to successfully solve engineering and design needs."}, {"h": "Primary Responsibilities", "t": "Leads large-scale project design by serving as a technical lead for complex assignments and managing the design from initial design to project completion.\nExecutes high-level analysis and review of project documents ensuring compliance with applicable standards, codes, and regulations.\nOversees and regularly monitors engineering processes and resources to maximize productivity and efficiency.\nDevelops and implements standards and guidelines for diverse engineering activities to ensure high-quality results.\nElevates the level of technical expertise within the team through technical design training and mentoring.\nSupports project management objectives by providing leadership and direction regarding organizing technical resources for key projects and utilizing resources effectively.\nCollaborates with project managers to ensure technical aspects of projects are completed on time, within budget, and meet established objectives.\nDemonstrates an elevated degree of creativity, decision-making, and responsibility for design tasks within a specific discipline."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "Strong communication skills.\nAbility to contribute and work well on a team.\nMaster's Degree in Structural Engineering or Civil or Architectural Engineering with a structural emphasis.\n12-20+ years of related Structural Engineering experience.\nMust be a registered professional and have at least four years of experience supervising technical personnel.\nProven track record in meeting and exceeding client expectations through technical design work.\nExcellent client service orientation.\nSolid interpersonal and decision-making skills and the ability to generate innovative and effective solutions to complex problems."}, {"h": "#LI-RS1", "t": "The typical annual salary range for this role is as listed below. Compensation may vary based on geographic location, experience, and qualifications. Employees in this role may be eligible for our performance‑based bonus and merit increases."}, {"h": "$118,000 — $200,000 USD", "t": "Additional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["project-management", "training"]}, "ff0eaea66f": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nJoin Olsson’s South Facilities Engineering and Design team and help deliver high‑performing buildings across healthcare, education, data centers, laboratories, commercial, and federal markets. You’ll take on meaningful design ownership, coordinate across disciplines, and see your work through construction—growing your technical depth and leadership while contributing to a diverse set of complex facility projects that make a real impact."}, {"h": "Primary responsibilities", "t": "Own design packages for building structural systems (steel, concrete, masonry, light gage) including gravity and lateral analysis, calculations, and details.\nProduce and check drawings and models in Revit/AutoCAD; coordinate diligently with architectural, MEP, and site/civil teams for a fully integrated set.\nApply codes and standards (IBC, ASCE 7, ACI 318, AISC 360) to ensure safe, constructible, and cost‑effective designs.\nSupport project planning—estimate level of effort, sequence design tasks, and help maintain scope, schedule, and quality commitments.\nParticipate in QA/QC by performing self‑checks and peer reviews; incorporate redlines and lessons learned to elevate deliverables.\nEngage during construction—review submittals/RFIs, conduct site observations, and document field findings that inform design improvements.\nMentor junior engineers and technicians through task guidance, model setup, and standards adoption.\nContribute to proposals (scope notes, resumes, past performance) and occasional client meetings to support team growth"}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "Bachelor’s degree in civil/structural engineering or related field.\nProfessional Engineer (PE) license required.\n4 or more years of structural design experience on building projects.\nProficiency with Revit/AutoCAD and familiarity with structural analysis tools (e.g., RISA, STAAD, SAP2000/ETABS).\nStrong knowledge of applicable codes/standards (IBC, ASCE 7, ACI, AISC).\nExcellent communication, organization, and problem‑solving skills; ability to lead tasks and mentor others."}, {"h": "#LI-DD1", "t": "Additional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["autocad", "building-codes", "concrete-design", "construction-administration", "etabs", "fea", "mep", "project-management", "quality-control", "revit", "seismic-design", "steel-design", "structural-analysis"]}, "99e5152328": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nOlsson's Facility Engineering and Design Team is at the forefront of engineering innovation, providing comprehensive services for large commercial developments, healthcare facilities, laboratories, educational institutions, data centers, and military installations.\n\nOur expertise includes engineering analysis, design services, and professional consulting, ensuring top-tier quality and world class installations. As a member of this team, you will contribute to diverse, high-impact projects, delivering engineering solutions that make a tangible difference in communities and industries.\nJoin Olsson's dynamic vertical infrastructure team, focusing on facilities engineering and design, as a Structural Project Engineer. In this role, you'll play a pivotal part on our team, contributing to a variety of challenging and innovative projects. Your responsibilities will involve designing and implementing structural solutions that meet both client and organizational needs, leveraging your expertise to deliver high-quality results in a collaborative environment."}, {"h": "Key responsibilities", "t": "Design and develop structural components for facility projects, ensuring compliance with industry standards and project specifications.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to integrate structural designs with other project elements.\nConduct structural analysis and prepare detailed reports.\nParticipate in project meetings, contributing technical insights and solutions.\nManage project timelines and resources, ensuring timely delivery and quality of work.\nStay abreast of advancements in structural engineering to apply innovative solutions in projects."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "Strong communication skills.\nAbility to contribute and work well on a team.\nExcellent interpersonal and problem-solving skills.\nBachelor's degree in civil or architectural engineering (structural emphasis)\nExperience utilizing structural design and drafting software packages preferred.\n6 years or more years of relevant experience.\nMust be a registered professional engineer."}, {"h": "#LI-DD1", "t": "Additional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["fea", "revit", "structural-analysis"]}, "7424c75322": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nOlsson is seeking a highly skilled and motivated Project Structural Engineer to join our Federal Engineering and Design Team, where your expertise will directly support the development of mission-critical infrastructure across the country. From military installations and VA hospitals to federal campuses and secure facilities, you’ll help shape the structural backbone of projects that serve national interests and improve lives.\nThis is more than a design role — it’s an opportunity to lead, collaborate, and innovate within a team that values technical excellence, client service, and community impact.\nAs a Project Structural Engineer, you’ll take ownership of structural design and coordination across a range of federal projects. Your day-to-day will include:\nLead structural engineering efforts for vertical infrastructure projects including barracks, hospitals, administrative buildings, and specialized federal facilities.\nPerform detailed structural analysis and design of steel, concrete, masonry, and wood systems. Develop construction documents including plans, specifications, and calculations.\nWork closely with architects, civil engineers, mechanical/electrical teams, and federal stakeholders to ensure seamless integration of structural systems.\nApply design standards including UFC (Unified Facilities Criteria), IBC (International Building Code), ASCE, AISC, and other federal and industry codes.\nSupport proposal writing, scope development, and participate in federal RFP responses to help grow Olsson’s federal portfolio.\nProvide technical guidance to junior engineers, review work for quality and accuracy, and foster a collaborative learning environment.\nWhy Olsson?\nContribute to projects that serve national interests and make a difference in communities.\nChoose from remote, hybrid, or in-office arrangements that support your lifestyle and productivity.\nJoin a team that values mentorship, innovation, and shared success. We celebrate wins together and learn from challenges.\nAdvance your career through leadership roles, technical training, and exposure to high-profile federal clients."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities.\nWe’re looking for candidates who bring both technical expertise and leadership potential."}, {"h": "Preferred qualifications", "t": "Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Civil or Architectural Engineering with a structural emphasis.\nPE or SE license (required).\n6+ years of experience in structural design, ideally with federal clients or projects.\nProficiency in Autodesk, Revit, and similar analysis tools.\nFamiliarity with DoD, VA, and federal design standards and processes.\nStrong communication skills, with the ability to lead meetings, coordinate teams, and engage with clients.\nExperience managing project schedules, budgets, and deliverables is a plus."}, {"h": "#LI-HH1", "t": "Additional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["building-codes", "construction-documents", "fea", "procurement", "project-management", "revit", "steel-design", "structural-analysis"]}, "ecd721f86a": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nOlsson's Facilities Engineering and Design Team is at the forefront of engineering innovation, providing comprehensive services for large commercial developments, healthcare facilities, laboratories, educational institutions, data centers, and military installations.\n\nOur expertise includes engineering analysis, design services, and professional consulting, ensuring top-tier quality and world class installations. We also provide building inspection and forensic investigation services.\n\nAs a member of this team, you will contribute to diverse, high-impact projects, delivering engineering solutions that make a tangible difference in communities and industries.\nAs a Senior Structural Engineer on our North Central Facilities Engineering and Design team, you will manage the design production of projects by leading staff to complete projects in accordance with the project schedule as well as providing high level technical support for other engineers on the project team.\n\nYou will lead project quality assurance/quality control (QA/QC) activities. You will act as an advisor on complex projects and apply advanced experience to make recommendations and decisions regarding project design work."}, {"h": "Primary responsibilities", "t": "Lead structural design for varied and complex projects, integrating innovative engineering solutions across multiple materials (steel, concrete, wood, masonry).\nSupervise and mentor junior engineers, fostering skill development and professional growth.\nPerform advanced structural analyses and present findings in clear, comprehensive reports.\nContribute to the production of a project when needed.\nPerform QA/QC and ensure delivery of completed designs meets quality standards and project objectives.\nCollaborate closely with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless project integration and promote efficiencies.\nContribute to the development of standards and/or guidelines for engineering activities within the team.\nEngage with clients to understand technical needs, provide strategic insights, and support business development by showcasing Olsson’s technical capabilities and expertise."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "Strong communication skills.\nAbility to contribute and work well on a team.\nBachelor’s degree in Civil or Architectural Engineering.\nMasters degree in Civil or Architectural Engineering (structural emphasis) is preferred, but not required.\nMust be a registered professional engineer.\n12 – 20+ years of relevant experience.\nExperience utilizing structural design and drafting software packages.\nProficient in Autodesk Revit.\n#LI-RS1 #LI-Hybrid\nAdditional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["business-development", "qa-testing", "quality-control", "revit", "structural-analysis"]}, "baa26772fc": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nOlsson’s Facility Engineering and Design Team is a recognized leader in delivering innovative, high-performance solutions for complex projects across multiple sectors—including large commercial developments, healthcare facilities, laboratories, educational institutions, data centers, and military installations. Our team combines engineering analysis, design expertise, and consulting services to ensure world-class quality and reliability.\nAs a Senior Structural Engineer , you will be a trusted technical leader and mentor, guiding teams through challenging projects that demand creativity, precision, and collaboration. This role is ideal for an experienced engineer who thrives on complexity, excels in diverse environments, and is passionate about shaping the next generation of engineering talent."}, {"h": "What you’ll do", "t": "Lead structural design for varied and complex projects, integrating innovative engineering solutions across multiple materials (steel, concrete, wood, masonry).\nSupervise and mentor junior engineers, fostering skill development and professional growth.\nPerform advanced structural analyses and present findings in clear, comprehensive reports.\nOversee project management, ensuring adherence to timelines, budgets, and quality standards.\nCollaborate closely with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless project integration.\nStay current with advancements in structural engineering and incorporate cutting-edge practices.\nEngage with clients to understand technical needs, provide strategic insights, and support business development by showcasing Olsson’s technical capabilities and expertise."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "Strong communication and leadership skills.\nAbility to manage complex projects and mentor engineering teams.\nMaster’s degree in Civil or Architectural Engineering (structural emphasis) preferred.\nMinimum of 8 years of structural engineering experience (preferred: 12+ years) with a focus on facilities design and project leadership.\nProfessional Engineer (PE) license required.\nProficiency in structural design and drafting software; experience with Autodesk Revit preferred."}, {"h": "#LI-DD1", "t": "Additional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["business-development", "concrete-design", "project-management", "revit", "structural-analysis"]}, "d4c4fcef34": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nAs a Senior Structural Engineer at Olsson, you will work with some of the world’s largest technology companies and other mission-critical clients. You will independently handle engineering and project management tasks on small to medium-sized projects, from conception to completion.\n\nYour responsibilities will include processing design calculations, develop project scopes and schedules, and producing structural construction drawings and specifications. Experience in the Data Center industry is preferred. You will also coordinate with other Olsson teams, professional staff, technical staff, and clients.\n*We have one opening and will consider candidates interested in being hybrid, working remotely, or working out of any Olsson office location regions/areas."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "Strong communication skills\nAbility to contribute and work well on a team\nMasters degree in Civil or Architectural Engineering (structural emphasis) is preferred, but not required\nExperience utilizing structural design and drafting software packages preferred\n9+ years of relevant experience"}, {"h": "Revit experience required", "t": "Must be a registered professional engineer"}, {"h": "#LI-DD1", "t": "#Remote\nAdditional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["construction-documents", "project-management", "revit", "structural-analysis"]}, "2d1cfaf120": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Category: Architecture & Construction Location: JOB TITLE: RemoteStructural Engineer (AutoCADDrafting & Structural Design & Calculations) Industry: Building &Construction Rate: 10 – 12AUD/hour Duration: 30 hours per week About theRole: Weare seeking a skilled and detail-oriented Structural Engineer to join a growingAustralian structural design firm.\n\nThe successful candidate will handleend-to-end design and drafting tasks from sketches provided by the Director,through to complete structural drawings ready for review. This is a remoterole, with flexible working hours aligned to Australian business operations. Qualifications: Must have a relevant experience as an AutoCAD Drafter.\n\nExperience using Structural Toolkit and/or CLEAR Calcs (preferred; CLEAR Calcs training available). Strong knowledge ofdrainage design including onsite detention and understanding of Australian residentialconstruction & engineering practices in AU is a MUST .\n\nWritten and verbal communication skills - needed for communicating with a range of people, both internally and externally Ability todraft, setup sheets and complete structural calculations Ability to work independently, stay on task, and meet project deadlines The ability to multitask and prioritize your workload Excellent attention to detail and accuracy in work Previous remote work experience with Australian clients.\n\nReliable internet connection and suitable home office setup.\n\nDuties and Responsibilities: · Drafting 2D/3D structural drawings using AutoCAD . ·Preparing detailed structural calculations using StructuralToolkit and/or CLEAR Calcs. ·Setting up jobs using pre-prepared templates and ensuring alldrawings are accurate and compliant with engineering principles. ·Translatedirector provided sketches to complete structural documentation ·Incorporating revisions and finalizing drawings for clientsubmission. ·Maintaining organized drawing files and project documentation. ·Communicating with the Director for clarification and approvals(no client-facing work required).\n\nDetails Originally posted on Himalayas"}], "k": ["autocad", "operations", "structural-analysis"]}, "d0fd60b479": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "We are seeking an experienced Structural Engineer, for a role in our Brisbane office. You will be an integral member of our team delivering quality services on projects from around Australia.\nYou will be involved in structural design of building projects focused in the commercial, retail, health, industrial, high rise and education sectors."}, {"h": "Specifically", "t": "All aspects of design in structural engineering with a focus on Property and Building projects.\nPreparation of design sketches and details for drafting by technical staff and oversee the design development and documentation.\nLiaising with and coordinating various stakeholders including clients, local government, and authorities.\nMeet our client expectations of projects being delivered on time and with a high degree of accuracy.\nAttend site for inspections.\nWhat This Role Offers.\nA collaborative and supportive work environment.\nThe opportunity to work on high-profile projects with tier 1 developers."}, {"h": "Attractive salary package and benefits.", "t": "Personal and professional development."}, {"h": "Tertiary level qualifications in Civil/Structural Engineering.", "t": "Minimum 2-3years experience.\nStrong communication and liaison abilities to engage with clients and other engineers.\nStrong knowledge of applicable Australian Standards, Local Government Authority Standards, statutory and regulatory requirements.\nExposure to developing structural design across a range of project cycles utilising relevant standards and best practice methodologies.\nAt Colliers, we are enterprising. What sets us apart is not what we do, but how we do it. Our people are passionate, take personal responsibility and always do what’s right for our clients, people and communities. We accelerate their success by empowering them to think and act differently to drive exceptional results.\nWith circa 9,000 experts in Asia Pacific, our enterprising culture and decentralised operating model allows us to act with speed in local markets, seizing opportunities to innovate and accelerate the success of our clients and our people.\nOur collaborative culture sets us apart. We help experts become true specialists and provide the long-term structure and platform to accelerate their success.\nWe foster an environment in which everyone at Colliers feels respected and comfortable bringing their authentic selves to do their best work. It’s our people who set us apart and we actively recruit people who represent the diversity of the communities in which we operate. We take great pride in doing what’s right and operating in ways that benefit the business, our people, our clients, our communities, and the environment.\nExperts join experts, and we welcome you to join us as we lead the industry into the future.\nPlease apply with your CV or reach out to jasmine.mims@colliers.com for more information.\nPlease be advised that applications will only be accepted directly rather than via recruitment agencies."}], "k": ["structural-analysis"]}, "2f807b2cb0": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor of Science Degree in Civil Engineering, with an emphasis in Structural Engineering Professional Engineer License (PE/PEng) Minimum of 4 years of experience in structural engineering Experience with US building codes including IBC, ASCE 7, ACI and AISC Experience with Structural Engineering analysis software, Navisworks and Bluebeam Experience designing and analyzing traditional steel and concrete structures Excellent written and verbal communication skills Strong interpersonal skills Working Conditions and Requirements Your home location must be in USA Northwest Region (AK, ID, MT, OR, WA, WY) or Canada Employee to provide internet service as required at home to effectively meet project performance requirements Preferred Qualifications: MS degree in Civil Engineering with an emphasis in Structural Engineering or MS degree in Structural Engineering Experience in semi-conductor industrial or general industrial facilities Experience leading small teams Responsibilities: Position Summary As a Structural Engineering Professional, you will be an integral member of the design team counted on to perform a significant portion of Structural analysis and design for our projects.\n\nYou will need strong communication and interpersonal skills as you work closely with your Structural Lead, Structural Engineers, Structural Designers, and other disciplines.\n\nAs part of this team, you will help develop design concepts, complete the analysis and design, and work with our Designers to get the structural requirements communicated on design documents and in the model.\n\nIt is expected that you have a solid foundation in the fundamentals of Structural Engineering, knowledge of multiple subject areas, experience with US building codes including seismic provisions, understand how Structural design integrates with and impacts other disciplines, and are building understanding of business trends and industry issues and challenges.\n\nYou will be given as much responsibility as you are willing to take, and your opportunities for career growth will be limited only by your own motivation, capabilities, and attitude.\n\nDuties and Responsibilities Under general supervision, competently perform all conventional aspects of Structural Engineering analysis and design Plan and conduct work requiring judgement in the independent evaluation, selection, and adaptation of engineering techniques, procedures, and criteria Exercise sound engineering judgement and problem-solving skills, not hesitating to reach out to others for guidance or confirmation when questions arise Possess knowledge of principles and practices of lateral analysis and design (wind and seismic), including ability to apply required provisions of the building code Exhibit a high level of attention to detail and quality control Committed to checking your own work, reaching out to peers and seniors for guidance when questions arise Perform calculation checking of other engineers' work Take responsibility for managing workload, make and keep commitments, and take full ownership of assigned work Take complete ownership of your portion of the structural scope, reliably working to meet schedule, budget, and quality requirements You may be given tasks with ill-defined conditions of satisfaction, in which case you will be expected to take the initiative to determine what is needed to meet the project and client needs Clearly define your own scope and start to develop your ability to forecast the level of effort needed to complete that scope Be ready to identify scope change and escalate it to your structural lead Recognize when help is needed, reaching out to peers and senior engineers for guidance Work in a timely, accurate, and cost-effective manner with strong attention to detail Developing leadership skills Provide technical guidance, coaching, and/or mentorship to designers/drafters and less experienced engineers Be proactive in advancing workflows, systems, and tools within the structural discipline; embrace emerging technologies Working Conditions and Requirements Your home location must be in the USA Northwest Region (AK, ID, MT, OR, WA, WY) or Canada Employee to provide internet service as required at home to effectively meet project performance requirements Originally posted on Himalayas"}], "k": ["bluebeam", "building-codes", "fea", "navisworks", "quality-control", "seismic-design", "steel-design", "structural-analysis", "training"]}, "6439564e64": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nAs a Senior Engineer on our Railroad Bridge team, you will play a key role in the planning, design, and delivery of railroad bridge and structural projects.\n\nYou will work closely with project managers, technical leaders, and clients to develop practical engineering solutions while providing technical guidance and mentorship to less experienced engineers.\n\nThis position offers the opportunity to lead technical design efforts, contribute to project success, and help deliver high-quality solutions that meet client needs and project objectives."}, {"h": "Primary Responsibilities will include", "t": "Lead the structural analysis and design of railroad bridges and related structures for a variety of transportation projects.\nPrepare and review engineering calculations, plans, specifications, and technical reports to ensure quality and accuracy.\nProvide technical direction and mentorship to junior engineers and engineering staff.\nCoordinate with multidisciplinary teams to develop innovative and practical design solutions.\nSupport project planning efforts by assisting with scope development, scheduling, budgeting, and resource coordination.\nConduct quality control reviews and ensure compliance with applicable design standards, codes, and client requirements.\nCollaborate directly with clients, contractors, railroads, and regulatory agencies throughout project development and delivery.\nAssist with business development activities, including proposal preparation, client relationship management, and identifying opportunities for future work.\nMaintain comprehensive project documentation, including design files, calculations, correspondence, and technical deliverables."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Working collaboratively with others.\nHaving ownership in the work you do.\nUsing your talents to positively affect communities.\nMentoring and supporting the growth of developing engineers."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering, Structural Engineering, or a related engineering field.\nMinimum of 8 years of relevant experience supporting railroad bridge and structure design projects.\nStrong knowledge of railroad bridge design principles, structural analysis, and industry standards.\nExperience leading technical design efforts and coordinating project deliverables.\nExcellent communication, collaboration, and problem-solving skills.\nProven ability to build and maintain strong client relationships.\nProfessional Engineering (P.E.) license required.\nExperience with MicroStation, RISA 3D, and Bluebeam Revu.\nValid driver’s license and a good driving history.\nWillingness to work a flexible schedule and travel as required.\n#LI-Remote"}, {"h": "#LI-AF1", "t": "Additional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["account-management", "bluebeam", "bridge-design", "budgeting", "business-development", "etabs", "fea", "microstation", "project-management", "quality-control", "scheduling", "structural-analysis", "training"]}, "884f3573e8": {"s": [{"h": "Overview", "t": "Exercises independent judgment in evaluation, selection and use of standard techniques, and solves problems when encountered. A licensed engineer who works on a variety of projects on structural design, preparation of implementation documentation, coordination with clients and construction administration. Collaborates with the project team to organize and plan projects."}, {"h": "Responsibilities", "t": "Collaborates with project team to effectively execute structural engineering design and delivery of structural implementation documents\nMay coordinate early phase effort for determination of most appropriate structural framing system(s) and project criteria including building code, fire-rating, gravity/lateral loads and other unique requirements of the project\nPerforms effectively as a team member during design and/or construction phases\nMay prepare and/or review structural specifications for projects at each phase of delivery\nMaintains active awareness of the production schedule for responsible task(s)\nCoordinates structural CA effort including engineering site visitation, field report documentation, submittal review, response to project RFI’s, and review of structural change order requests\nRevises implementation documents from markups and/or instructions and reviews completed tasks at key intervals for accuracy/completeness\nReviews work of EIT staff\nDirects the work of structural drafting staff for implementation documentation\nUtilizes standard engineering practices and techniques to adjust and correlate data; recognizes and resolves discrepancies in results\nMay be responsible for communication with other disciplines, vendors and contractors to ensure incorporation of all information into project requirements\nParticipates in team meetings to discuss project issues, coordination with other disciplines and technical issues\nConsistently documents project meetings and telephone conversations\nMaintains knowledge of products and materials available on the market\nTravel may be required"}, {"h": "Education and Experience", "t": "Accredited professional degree in Civil, Structural or Architectural Engineering or related field\nTypically 5+ years of experience\nLicenses and Certifications\nProfessional engineering or structural engineering licensure required (structural engineering licensure preferred)\nKnowledge, Skills and Abilities\nAdvanced – expert-level experience, knowledge or skills\nIntermediate – experience, knowledge or skills required to produce high-quality solutions or work\nBasic – familiar with primary concepts or capabilities and may perform elementary functions depending on role\nIntermediate knowledge of software such as Revit and BIM required\nIntermediate knowledge of structural analytical software required\nIntermediate knowledge of MS Office Suite required\nIntermediate knowledge of building codes, material design standards, select structural standards, constructability, etc. required\nBasic knowledge of project management tools (Vision, Portfolio, etc.) preferred\nIntermediate knowledge of integrated design, engineering building systems and QA/QC process required\nIntermediate ability to communicate in a clear, concise and professional manner both verbally and in writing required\nIntermediate ability to problem solve and apply innovative solutions required\nIntermediate ability to work and collaborate in a team environment required\nIntermediate ability to work on multiple projects at the same time required\nIntermediate ability to effectively meet deadlines at expected quality required\nBase Salary Range: $84k - $105k annually - Chicago locations only.\nThe estimate displayed represents the general base salary range of candidates hired in the Chicago location only. We may ultimately pay more or less than the posted range based on the location of the role. Factors that may be used to determine your actual salary may include internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training.\nHKS offers a comprehensive total compensation & benefits package with health, dental, and vision care coverage, 401(k) plans, life & AD&D insurance, short/long term disability plans, paid days off (sick leave, parental leave, vacation), and much more for benefits-eligible employees. To learn more about our benefits visit this page.\nIf you currently work for HKS, please submit your application via the Internal Careers Portal .\nHKS is an EEO/AA Employer: M/F/Disabled/Veteran"}], "k": ["bim", "building-codes", "construction-administration", "project-management", "quality-control", "revit", "structural-analysis"]}, "b68d617203": {"s": [{"h": "Overview", "t": "A recognized practitioner and licensed engineer who possesses strong technical abilities and manages implementation documentation. Uses the firm’s resources (people, processes, and tools) and assignments with proficiency, fluency and aptitude. Teaches and mentors staff and effectively embodies and expresses the firm’s values and mission."}, {"h": "Responsibilities", "t": "Coordinates structural project team efforts to facilitate effective execution of structural engineering design and the delivery of structural implementation documents\nLeads early phase effort for determination of most appropriate structural framing system(s)\nEstablishes structural project criteria including building code, fire-rating, gravity/lateral loads and unique requirements of the project\nPerforms effectively as a senior team member during design and/or construction phases\nPrepares and/or reviews structural specifications for projects at each phase of delivery\nMaintains active awareness of the production schedule for responsible project(s)\nEstablishes credibility through project management skills\nEffectively manages structural CA effort including engineering site visitation, field report documentation, submittal review, response to project RFI’s, and review of structural change order requests\nReviews implementation documents at key phases/intervals for accuracy and completeness.\nSupervises junior project team members, both engineering and drafting staff. Delegates appropriate tasks, answers questions, and holds junior project team members accountable.\nReviews staff performance relative to project contributions on a regular basis in a constructive manner to strengthen team(s)\nUtilizes standard engineering practices and techniques to adjust and correlate data; recognizes and resolves discrepancies in results\nResponsible for communication with other disciplines, clients, vendors and contractors to ensure incorporation of all information into project requirements\nParticipates in and leads team meetings to discuss project issues, coordination with other disciplines and technical issues\nConsistently documents project meetings and telephone conversations\nMaintains up to date knowledge of products and materials available on the market\nTravel will be required"}, {"h": "Education and Experience", "t": "Accredited professional degree in Civil, Structural or Architectural Engineering or related field\nTypically 7+ years of experience\nLicenses and Certifications\nProfessional engineering or structural engineering licensure required (structural engineering licensure preferred)"}, {"h": "Ability to be licensed in multiple states preferred", "t": "Knowledge, Skills and Abilities\nAdvanced – expert-level experience, knowledge or skills\nIntermediate – experience, knowledge or skills required to produce high-quality solutions or work\nBasic – familiar with primary concepts or capabilities and may perform elementary functions depending on role\nAdvanced understanding on the use of Revit and BIM in the delivery of implementation documents required\nIntermediate knowledge of MS Office Suite required\nAdvanced knowledge of building codes and material design standards required\nAdvanced knowledge in select structural systems required\nAdvanced technical knowledge through a combination of academic experience, work experience and continuing education required\nBasic knowledge of project management tools (Vision, Portfolio, etc.) preferred\nIntermediate knowledge of integrated design, engineering building systems and QA/QC process required\nAdvanced organizational skills and the ability to work on multiple projects at the same time required\nAdvanced ability to exercise judgment and discretion, set priorities and manage competing demands required\nAdvanced ability to communicate in a clear, concise and professional manner both verbally and in writing required\nAdvanced ability to problem solve and apply innovative solutions required\nAdvanced ability to work and encourage collaboration in a team environment required\nAdvanced ability to work on multiple projects at the same time required\nAdvance ability to effectively meet deadlines at expected quality required\nBase Salary Range: $99k - $141k annually - Chicago and Washington DC locations only.\nThe estimate displayed represents the general base salary range of candidates hired in the Chicago and Washington DC locations only. We may ultimately pay more or less than the posted range based on the location of the role. Factors that may be used to determine your actual salary may include internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training.\nHKS offers a comprehensive total compensation & benefits package with health, dental, and vision care coverage, 401(k) plans, life & AD&D insurance, short/long term disability plans, paid days off (sick leave, parental leave, vacation), and much more for benefits-eligible employees. To learn more about our benefits visit this page.\nIf you currently work for HKS, please submit your application via the Internal Careers Portal .\nHKS is an EEO/AA Employer: M/F/Disabled/Veteran"}], "k": ["bim", "building-codes", "project-management", "quality-control", "revit"]}, "a222928a3e": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "You will have expertise in independently performing analysis and preparing Structural designs for a wide range of facilities of the type as would commonly be found on a DoD Installation.\nYou will have expertise in developing complex Structural designs and analysis utilizing engineering software and drawings in Auto Cad and REVIT.\nYou will possess in-depth knowledge of specifications, criteria, policy, industry criteria and standards, and standard practices as related to Structural Engineering.\nYou will be able to provide leadership and specialized engineering consultation and support to the NAVFAC SE Structural Engineering community.\nYou will have expertise in ensuring that the Structural aspects of projects are constructed in accordance with the contract plans and specifications.\nYou will be proficient in the following construction support activities: Review and Approve shop drawings, Delegated Designs, Value Engineering Cost Proposals (VECPs), and provide technical responses to Requests for Information (RFIs).\nYou will have expertise in developing Architect and Engineering Statements of Work and providing design, scope, and budget oversite for projects.\nThis position has a Selective Placement Factor (SPF). You must have a current registration as a Professional Engineer (PE) from any state, the District of Columbia, Guam or Puerto Rico. If you meet this requirement, you must provide a copy of your current registration with your application.\n\nA copy of a wall certificate that does not show current registration status will not serve to verify you meet this requirement.\n\nIn addition to the SPF, your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-12 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector performing the following duties: 1) Providing structural engineering analysis and expertise for designs on a wide range of complex projects on new and existing facilities; 2) Preparing work drawings and technical specifications for the structural portion on construction projects; 3) Performing field investigations to verify and document existing conditions as a basis for the design for new/existing projects; 4) Providing technical specifications and assisting with detailed labor and material cost estimates for use in obtaining project funding for bid evaluation; and 5) Managing assigned projects from cradle to grave for adherence to budget, schedule, and quality standards.\n\nNOTE: This information must be fully supported in your resume.\n\nAdditional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=Overview and https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/0800/civil-engineering-series-0810/ Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social).\n\nVolunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment."}], "k": ["autocad", "cad-drafting", "construction-administration", "criminal-investigation", "revit"]}, "f452b5f5fa": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "DLR Group is an integrated design firm with a promise to elevate the human experience through design. This fuels the work we do around the world and inspires our mission to improve the lives of our clients, our communities, and our planet. If this sparks your interest, you’re in the right place.\nDLR Group has an exciting opportunity for a Senior Structural Engineer + National Quality Control (NQC) Leader. This hybrid leadership role combines technical structural engineering expertise with national quality leadership responsibilities.\nAs the National Quality Control Leader and Senior Structural Engineer, you will lead quality control initiatives and continuously advance QC processes and best practices across DLR Group's structural engineering practice. In addition, you will design and oversee structural systems from schematic design through construction administration for a diverse portfolio of building types, collaborating with multidisciplinary teams to deliver high-quality, innovative design solutions."}, {"h": "National Quality Control Leader", "t": "Lead the advancement of quality control initiatives across DLR Group’s Structural Engineering practice by developing, implementing, and continuously improving QC processes and standards.\nChampion a culture of technical excellence by integrating lessons learned, industry best practices, and innovative approaches into engineering processes and project delivery.\nCollaborate with regional and national engineering leaders to establish consistent quality standards, review practices, and continuous improvement strategies across the firm.\nDevelop and maintain QC procedures, training resources, and best practice guidelines to support engineering teams and promote consistent application across projects.\nProvide mentorship and training to engineers, quality control reviewers, and technical leaders to strengthen review processes and enhance project outcomes.\nFacilitate project quality reviews and audits to evaluate compliance, identify opportunities for improvement, and communicate key insights to leadership.\nPartner with project teams across multiple regions to support independent quality reviews, encourage knowledge sharing, and strengthen collaboration across the Structural Engineering practice.\nParticipate in DLR Group’s Integrated Practice QC Work Group to help shape and implement firmwide quality initiatives.\nTrack and communicate QC performance metrics, trends, and recommendations to engineering leadership to support continuous improvement.\nShare quality initiatives, lessons learned, and best practices with the broader engineering community through discipline meetings and firmwide forums."}, {"h": "Senior Structural Engineer", "t": "Strive for excellence in developing structural solutions from concept through construction.\nBe a decision-maker in developing system layouts, narratives, calculations and engineering reports.\nWelcome deep collaboration with architects, other engineers, and clients as part of our integrated design process.\nLearn and adapt to variations in building codes and construction practices while working on projects around the US.\nProduce construction documents using Revit.\nAssist contractors by reviewing shop drawings, RFIs and participating in O/A/C meetings.\nPass along knowledge by mentoring entry-level staff.\nPromote workflow and technical standards best-practices for our diverse multi-office practice.\nContribute to managing the operations, execution, and expectations for the Structural Engineering Discipline in Colorado.\nSupport business development initiatives by assisting the RFP process, participating in project interviews, and actively engaging in community and/or industry specific organization that will build the DLR Group brand."}, {"h": "Required Qualifications", "t": "Bachelor's degree in Civil/Structural/Architectural Engineering; Master’s degree preferred.\n8-15 years of building related structural engineering experience, including the design of concrete, masonry, steel and wood/timber; gravity and lateral systems.\nLicensed Professional Engineer (PE) Licensed Structural Engineer (SE) preferred.\nPrior experience leading teams of engineers on projects.\nWorking knowledge of current structural software (ETABS, SAP, SAFE, RAM, ADAPT, RISA, Enercalc).\nExperience with BIM including Autodesk Revit workflow.\nGoal oriented with strong skills in problem solving, creativity, and attention to detail.\nUnderstanding of commercial building materials, systems, and assemblies.\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills.\nPassion for sustainable building design and SE2050 commitment.\nExperience with directing and coordinating project activities of junior staff.\nOur comprehensive Benefits at DLR Group include medical, dental, vision, disability, wellness programs, flex spending, paid holidays, and paid time off. We also offer a 401(k) plan, employee stock ownership, and bonus opportunities. Compensation considerations are based on location, experience, and skills. The suggested hourly rate for this position is:\nHourly Rate"}, {"h": "$84,700 — $144,430 USD", "t": "DLR Group is an integrated design firm delivering architecture, engineering, interiors, planning, and building optimization for new builds, renovations, and adaptive reuse projects.\nWe are 100% employee-owned: every employee is literally invested in our clients’ success. At the core of our firm are interdisciplinary teams engaged in every step of project lifecycles.\n\nOur teams champion true collaboration, open information sharing, shared risk and reward, value-based decision making, and proficient use of technology to deliver exceptional design. We are pursuing the goals of the 2030 Challenge, the ME2040, and the SE2050, and are an initial signatory of the China Accord and the AIA 2030 Commitment.\nThrough our values – commitment, creativity, environmental stewardship, fun, integrity, ownership, sharing, teamwork – we elevate the human experience through design, together.\nDLR Group follows a four-day in-office work model, with employees having the flexibility to work somewhere other than the office on Fridays.\nWe are proud to be an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/M/F/Veteran/Disabled employer."}], "k": ["bim", "building-codes", "business-development", "cad-drafting", "construction-administration", "construction-documents", "etabs", "lean-six-sigma", "procurement", "project-management", "quality-control", "revit", "sap", "training"]}, "bb92971ab5": {"s": [{"h": "Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications", "t": "Bachelor of Science Degree in Civil Engineering, with an emphasis in Structural Engineering\nProfessional Engineer License (PE/PEng)\nMinimum of 10 years of experience in structural engineering\nProficient with US building codes, including IBC, ASCE 7, ACI and AISC\nProficient with Structural Engineering analysis software, Navisworks and Bluebeam\nProficient with designing and analyzing traditional steel and concrete structures\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills\nStrong interpersonal skills"}, {"h": "Preferred Qualifications", "t": "MS degree in Civil Engineering with an emphasis in Structural Engineering or MS degree in Structural Engineering\nStructural Engineer License (SE)\nExperience in semi-conductor industrial or general industrial facilities\nExperience leading medium teams"}, {"h": "Working Conditions and Requirements", "t": "Your home location must be in USA Southwest Region (AZ, CA, CO, HI, NM, NV, UT) or Canada\nEmployee to provide internet service as required at home to effectively meet project performance requirements\nResponsibilities: Position Summary As a Structural Engineering Professional, you will be an integral member of the design team counted on to perform a significant portion of Structural analysis and design for our projects.\n\nYou will need strong communication and interpersonal skills as you work closely with your Structural Lead, Structural Engineers, Structural Designers, and other disciplines.\n\nAs part of this team, you will help develop design concepts, complete the analysis and design, and work with our Designers to get the structural requirements communicated on design documents and in the model.\n\nIt is expected that you have a solid foundation in the fundamentals of Structural Engineering, knowledge of multiple subject areas; experience with US building codes, including seismic provisions; understand how Structural design integrates with and impacts other disciplines; and are building understanding of business trends and industry issues and challenges.\n\nThis position may require you to serve as a Lead Structural Engineer for medium-sized projects or as a Sub Lead for larger projects. You will be given as much responsibility as you are willing to take, and your opportunities for career growth will be limited only by your own motivation, capabilities, and attitude. Duties and Responsibilities\nWith little or no supervision, competently perform all conventional aspects of Structural Engineering analysis and design\nPlan and conduct work requiring judgement in the independent evaluation, selection, and adaptation of engineering techniques, procedures, and criteria\nExercise sound engineering judgement and problem-solving skills, not hesitating to reach out to others for guidance or confirmation when questions arise\nPossess strong knowledge of principles and practices of lateral analysis and design (wind and seismic), including ability to apply required provisions of the building code\nExhibit a high level of attention to detail and quality control\nCommitted to checking your own work, reaching out to peers and seniors for guidance when questions arise\nPerform calculation checking of other engineers' work\nTake responsibility for managing workload, make and keep commitments, and take full ownership of assigned work\nTake complete ownership of your portion of the structural scope, reliably working to meet schedule, budget, and quality requirements\nYou may be given tasks with ill-defined conditions of satisfaction, in which case you will be expected to take the initiative to determine what is needed to meet the project and client needs\nClearly define your own scope and forecast level of effort needed to complete that scope\nBe ready to identify scope change and escalate it to your Structural Lead or Project Manager\nRecognize when help is needed, reaching out to peers and senior engineers for guidance\nWork in a timely, accurate, and cost-effective manner with strong attention to detail\nDeveloping leadership skills\nProvide technical guidance, coaching, and/or mentorship to designers/drafters and less experienced engineers\nBe proactive in advancing workflows, systems, and tools within the structural discipline; embrace emerging technologies\nOriginally posted on Himalayas"}], "k": ["bluebeam", "building-codes", "fea", "navisworks", "quality-control", "seismic-design", "steel-design", "structural-analysis", "training"]}, "fb9eb130ae": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Company Description\nWe are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.\nWe’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.\nJob Description\nJoin our dynamic industrial team at Olsson, where we combine innovation with excellence in the industrial sector. Recognized as one of the \" Best Places to Work ,\" Olsson provides a collaborative environment for engineers to lead diverse challenges and contribute to impactful projects.\n\nWe serve a diverse client base ranging from local municipalities to private industry, creating opportunities to explore different sectors, project types, and career interests. Opportunities include agricultural , advanced manufacturing , semiconductors , mining , pharmaceuticals , wastewater , and bioenergy .\nAt Olsson, we believe in Engineering Possibilities by turning client ideas into reality while empowering our teams to innovate, grow, and make a lasting impact across evolving industries.\nWe are seeking an Associate Structural Engineer with strong technical curiosit y and a desire to grow their engineering skills. In this role, you'll work with a team of experienced engineers to deliver projects, solve complex challenges, and take on increasing responsibility in engineering analysis, design, and project coordination.\n\nAs a continuing developmental Engineer-in-Training (EIT), you'll apply established engineering principles, contribute to practical design solutions, and continue building the technical and professional skills needed for long-term career growth."}, {"h": "Primary Duties and Responsibilities", "t": "Design Solutions by developing calculations, models, and construction documents to deliver safe, practical industrial facilities.\nDeliver Projects by supporting design, coordination, and project documentation for successful project outcomes.\nSolve Challenges by applying engineering principles and collaborating with experienced engineers to develop effective solutions.\nCollaborate Across Teams with engineers, designers, clients, and contractors to advance project goals.\nGrow Your Expertise through hands-on experience with structural analysis, design software, and real-world projects.\nSupport Quality Delivery by preparing calculations, reports, and documentation that meet project requirements.\nDevelop Others by mentoring interns and sharing technical knowledge.\nGain Field Experience through site visits that verify conditions and support design and construction activities."}, {"h": "You are passionate about", "t": "Collaborating with coworkers to develop custom, impactful solutions for clients.\nPlaying an active role in project success – from understanding scope, contributing to designs, and creation of project documents.\nContinuously learning and developing new skills to grow as an engineer.\nSupporting the industries that keep our communities strong.\nWorking in a fast-paced environment where each day brings new challenges and opportunities.\nAdvancing team goals through a willingness to take on new challenges."}, {"h": "You bring to the team", "t": "Strong communication skills.\nAbility to contribute and work well with a team.\nExcellent interpersonal and problem-solving skills.\nBachelor’s degree in Civil or Architectural Engineering with a Structural emphasis.\nA minimum of one year of engineering experience.\nMust possess an Engineer Intern (EI) certificate.\nExperience developing detailed 3D models and construction documentation in Autodesk Revit.\nFamiliar with ACAD Software, RISA 3D, EnerCalc, MS Excel, and Hilti/Dewalt design."}, {"h": "#LI-DD1", "t": "Additional Information\nOlsson specializes in engineering and design, client advisory services, planning, field services, and environmental. Improving the world has been our mindset from the very beginning, back when Olsson first opened for business in 1956. And it will be our mindset for years to come."}, {"h": "As an Olsson employee, you will", "t": "Receive a competitive 401(k) match\nBe empowered to build your career with tailored development paths\nHave the possibility for flexible work arrangements\nEngage in work that has a positive impact on communities\nParticipate in a wellness program promoting balanced lifestyles\nIn addition, full-time employees will receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.) and the opportunity to participate in a bonus system that rewards performance.\nOlsson is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage qualified minority, female, veteran, and disabled candidates to apply and be considered for open positions. We do not discriminate against any applicant for employment or any employee because of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender, disability, age, military status, or other protected status.\nOlsson understands the importance of privacy and is committed to protecting job applicants’ personal information. Pursuant to the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (collectively, the “CCPA”), this notice explains Olsson’s practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal information for job applicants residing in California. Please read this Notice carefully to understand our privacy practices.\nFor more information about the types of information we collect and how we use it in connection with your general access and use of our website, please review our general California Privacy Notice here ."}], "k": ["3d-modeling", "construction-documents", "etabs", "excel", "fea", "project-management", "revit", "structural-analysis", "training"]}, "6ac1dde0f1": {"s": [{"h": "%PDF-1.7%����", "t": "11 0 obj endobj\nxref\n11 43\n0000000016 00000 n\n0000001414 00000 n\n0000001578 00000 n\n0000001620 00000 n\n0000002736 00000 n\n0000002761 00000 n\n0000002896 00000 n\n0000003332 00000 n\n0000003367 00000 n\n0000003480 00000 n\n0000003564 00000 n\n0000003945 00000 n\n0000004448 00000 n\n0000005418 00000 n\n0000006242 00000 n\n0000006782 00000 n\n0000006870 00000 n\n0000007372 00000 n\n0000007980 00000 n\n0000008568 00000 n\n0000008741 00000 n\n0000009658 00000 n\n0000010315 00000 n\n0000010968 00000 n\n0000011439 00000 n\n0000012030 00000 n\n0000012889 00000 n\n0000015538 00000 n\n0000019286 00000 n\n0000023769 00000 n\n0000023857 00000 n\n0000024312 00000 n\n0000024604 00000 n\n0000024910 00000 n\n0000024994 00000 n\n0000027993 00000 n\n0000028365 00000 n\n0000028836 00000 n\n0000037202 00000 n\n0000037239 00000 n\n0000037817 00000 n\n0000075742 00000 n\n0000001