neer — Help Shape Communities While Growing Your Career with KPFF\nFull-time\nDiscipline : Structural Engineering\nCompany Description\n\nWho We Are\n\nAt KPFF, we believe great engineering starts with great people. As a nationally recognized, employee-owned engineering firm, we deliver impactful projects across the country while staying deeply connected to the communities we serve.\n\nOur Birmingham team offers something increasingly rare: the opportunity to continue building an established career close to home while working on innovative, high-profile projects nationwide. Whether you are looking to return to Birmingham, deepen your local roots, or take the next step in your structural engineering journey, KPFF offers the reach and technical depth of a national firm with the culture and flexibility of a local team.\n\nAt KPFF, careers are shaped by initiative, mentorship, and leadership, not rigid corporate ladders. We invest heavily in developing future leaders through hands-on mentorship, technical collaboration, and opportunities to grow your career in the direction that matters most to you.\n\nLearn more at kpff.com.\n\nJob Description\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nWe are seeking an adaptive and thoughtful Structural Engineer with 4+ years of experience to join our growing Birmingham team.\n\nThis role offers the opportunity to build a meaningful career close to home while contributing to innovative structural engineering projects across the country. Whether you are looking to return to Birmingham, stay connected to the community you care about, or expand your career opportunities without leaving your hometown, KPFF offers the project diversity and reach of a national firm with the mentorship, support, and connection of a local team.\n\nIn this role, you will contribute to structural engineering projects from concept through construction while continuing to grow as a licensed professional. You will work with experienced engineers, BIM professionals, and clients, with mentorship and career support from KPFF’s engineering team.\n\nYou will take on meaningful project responsibilities, strengthen your technical and leadership skills, and contribute to impactful work locally and nationwide."}, {"h": "What You’ll Do", "t": "Manage all aspects of structural engineering projects, including planning, scheduling, budgeting, and resource allocation\nPerform structural analysis and design for a variety of building types and materials\nCollaborate with clients to understand project goals and maintain clear, consistent communication throughout the project lifecycle\nParticipate in feasibility studies, site investigations, and structural assessments, as needed\nPrepare, review, and coordinate engineering drawings, calculations, specifications, and reports in accordance with applicable building codes\nMonitor project progress, identify risks or challenges, and implement mitigation strategies to support successful outcomes\nSupport KPFF’s mission of creating a perpetual organization built on happy people, happy clients, strong financial outcomes, and great engineering\nPromote compliance with health, safety, and environmental regulations while fostering a culture of safety"}, {"h": "Qualifications", "t": "Professional Background\n\nBachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering or Architectural Engineering (Master’s preferred)\nProfessional Engineer (PE) license required\nMinimum 4 years of structural engineering design experience (project management experience is a plus)\nProficiency with structural analysis and design software such as ETABS, RAM Structural System, RISA‑3D, or similar\nStrong knowledge of applicable building codes and standards (IBC, ASCE, ACI, AISC)\nExperience with BIM software such as Revit\nStrong communication and interpersonal skills\nAbility to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines\nCommitment to continuous learning and professional development\nAdditional Information"}, {"h": "We Also Have Some Pretty Sweet Benefits!", "t": "At KPFF, we believe your growth goes beyond project work. We invest in every team member’s personal and professional development by offering generous paid time off to recharge, regular career check-ins to align goals and growth opportunities, and paid educational programs to support licensure and lifelong learning. Your success matters here — and we provide the time, resources, and mentorship to help you thrive.\n\nGenerous PTO & Holiday Pay – supporting your wellbeing and rest, including 2 flexible holidays.\nComprehensive Benefits – 2 healthcare options, dental, vision, flexible spending accounts, Employee Assistance Program (EAP), short- and long-term disability, life & ADD insurance.\nShort-Term/Impact Bonus: Impact Bonuses are distributed on a semi-annual basis and are consistent with role, impact, and Reporting Center performance.\nPaid Family Leave: KPFF provides paid time off to help take care of your loved ones.\nPaid Overtime - KPFF pays you for every hour you work and gives you the option to “bank” your time for later use as vacation or to be paid out once a month.\n401(k) with 3% Contribution – KPFF contributes whether you do or not!\nMentorship & Technical Excellence Programs – Through KPFF’s Forefront Education Program, you’ll receive unparalleled mentorship from seasoned professionals, empowering you to excel in your career from day one. Thrive in a setting that values your development and independence, where your ideas are welcomed, and your contributions make a real impact.\nPDH Budget – KPFF offers a bank of both funds and time to help further your education on an annual basis.\nPaid Exams, Memberships & Educational Opportunities – To help better support our team members, we provide reimbursement for the PE and SE exams, an annual membership budget, and also Reporting Center Wide educational opportunities for PDH hours.\nPE License Renewal – We pay for PE license renewals for 1 state/year.\nFlexible scheduling - core hours of collaboration are 8:30-4:30 PM.\nPaid Parking – KPFF provides parking or reimbursement for public transit for all team members.\nA fun, collaborative, and inclusive culture that values people first."}, {"h": "Physical and Work Environment", "t": "Work is typically conducted in an office setting, with frequent use of a computer.\nOccasional lifting up to 15 lbs."}, {"h": "#LI-AK1", "t": "KPFF Consulting Engineers participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the U.S.\n\nKPFF Consulting Engineers is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, creed, ethnicity, national origin, religion, marital status, sex/gender (including sexual orientation or gender identity), pregnancy, veteran status, citizenship status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected basis.\n\nBy clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply\n\nI'm interested\nPrivacy Notice\nCookies Settings\nI'm interested\nRefer a friend\n\nPosted by\n\nMegan Carr"}, {"h": "OTHER JOBS AT KPFF CONSULTING ENGINEERS", "t": "Structural Engineering Team Leader — Big Firm Opportunity, Local Influence\n\nMadison, WI\n\nStructural Engineer — Help Shape Communities While Growing Your Career with KPFF"}], "k": ["account-management", "bim", "budgeting", "building-codes", "criminal-investigation", "etabs", "excel", "fea", "project-management", "revit", "scheduling", "steel-design", "structural-analysis"]}, "53122bef0e": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Press Alt+1 for screen-reader mode, Alt+0 to cancel\nAccessibility Screen-Reader Guide, Feedback, and Issue Reporting | New window\nJob Openings\n\nDegenkolb Engineers hires structural engineers at all phases of their careers as well as supporting positions in accounting, marketing, information technology, human resources, and legal consulting. Information on positions throughout the firm is located in the listings below.\n\nCaution Alert: Please be aware of imposter scams\n\nDegenkolb will never request sensitive personal information or payment during recruiting. Any legitimate request for onboarding information will only be sent securely through DocuSign after an official offer has been accepted.\n\nIndividuals may pose as company recruiters, using company names and logos to offer job opportunities and scam you out of money. These impostors ask for personal information such as Social Security numbers or banking details.\n\nIf you believe you’ve been contacted by an impersonator, do not share your information and report the incident to humanresources@degenkolb.com.\n\nAll locations\nDetroit, MI\nGrand Rapids, MI\nLos Angeles, CA\nOakland, CA\nOrange, CA\nSacramento, CA\nSan Diego, CA\nSan Francisco, CA\nSeattle, WA\n02-Entry-Level Structural Engineer | Designer\nEntry-Level Structural Engineer | DesignerNew !\n\nLos Angeles, CA\n\nPosition Description We review candidates for theEntry-Level Structural Engineer | Designerposition throughout the year on a rolling basis for all California offices - Los Angeles, Oakland, Orange County, Sacramento, San Diego, and San Francisco - as well as Seattle, Washington, and our Midwest offices in Detroit and Grand Rapids, Michigan. Launch your structural engineering career with meaningf..."}, {"h": "VIEW JOB DETAILS", "t": "Entry-Level Structural Engineer | DesignerNew !\n\nOakland, CA\n\nPosition Description We review candidates for theEntry-Level Structural Engineer | Designerposition throughout the year on a rolling basis for all California offices - Los Angeles, Oakland, Orange County, Sacramento, San Diego, and San Francisco - as well as Seattle, Washington, and our Midwest offices in Detroit and Grand Rapids, Michigan. Launch your structural engineering career with meaningf..."}, {"h": "VIEW JOB DETAIL