eral buildings. We address every project ne..."}, {"h": "VIEW JOB DETAILS", "t": "Structural Engineer | Design Engineer\n\nOakland, CA\n\nCompany Background:Founded in 1940 and headquartered in San Francisco, Degenkolb Engineers has more than eight decades of commitment to innovation, client service, and life-long learning.We deliver customized structural solutions in a variety ofpractice areassuch as healthcare, education, science and technology,forensics, construction engineering, and federal buildings. We address every project ne..."}, {"h": "VIEW JOB DETAILS", "t": "Structural Engineer | Design Engineer\n\nLos Angeles, CA\n\nCompany Background:Founded in 1940 and headquartered in San Francisco, Degenkolb Engineers has more than eight decades of commitment to innovation, client service, and life-long learning.We deliver customized structural solutions in a variety ofpractice areassuch as healthcare, education, science and technology,forensics, construction engineering, and federal buildings. We address every project ne..."}], "k": ["accessibility", "accounting", "bim", "business-development", "hr-operations", "revit"]}, "2589bfe9ab": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Skip to main content\nEN\nDE\nToggle Menu"}, {"h": "Your future colleague", "t": "Leonie Eitzenberger\nStructural Engineer (m/f/x) with or without experience\nApply Now"}, {"h": "HOME / JOBS", "t": "Our offer\nThe chance to play an active part in planning a sustainably designed environment\nChallenging assignments in an office with a team-based, interdisciplinary structure\nA permanent contract with long-term future prospects\nOpportunities for personal development and advancement within a global network\nClimate-friendly transport incentives (e.g. company bicycles and travel tickets)\nAn office in an attractive location with excellent public transport links\nGood teamwork, good working atmosphere and several annual team events\nJob Info\n\nLocation\nVienna\n\nCompany\nWerner Sobek Wien\n\nDepartment\nStructural Engineering\n\nExperience Level\nExperienced Professionals, Young Professionals\n\nShare this job"}, {"h": "Your responsibilities", "t": "Applying your engineering skills to help execute ambitious construction projects around the world\nProducing the calculations and conceptual designs for loadbearing and special structures\nClose cooperation with various disciplines within our company\nCommunicating with architectural practices, clients and contractors\nParticipation or organization of project meetings and site visits\nYour profile\nYou’ll have successfully completed your education as a civil engineer (majoring in structural engineering)\nYou’re a team player who may or may not have professional experience\nYou have strong powers of spatial visualization\nYou’re familiar with finite elements and CAD software\nYou speak fluent German and have a very good command of English"}, {"h": "You’re ready to take on responsibility and play an active role", "t": "Your application\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application along with your preferred starting date.\nIf you have any questions, please do not hesitate to get in touch.\n\nThe collectively agreed minimum gross salary for this position is 3.145 EUR p.m. (BG 4/1 for 40 h/Week) with a willingness to offer higher pay depending on qualifications and experience.\n\nApply Now\n\nJob Description PDF (2 MB)\n\nWerner Sobek Wien ZT GmbH\nPersonal/HR\nUngargasse 37\n1030 Vienna (AT)\nTel. +43.1.928 08 24-0\ncareer@wernersobek.com\nwww.wernersobek.com\n\nBelgrade\nBerlin\nBuenos Aires\nCopenhagen\nDubai\nFrankfurt\nHamburg\nIstanbul\nNew York\nRiyadh\nStuttgart\nTashkent\nVienna\nWeinheim"}, {"h": "About us", "t": "Services\nNews\nTopics\nFocus\nProjects\nCareer\nMedia\nNewsletter\nContact\nImprint\nPrivacy Policy\nDisclaimer\nEN\nDE\nThis button closes the dialog. Its functionality is identical to the Accept only essential cookies button.\nPrivacy Preference\n\nWe use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential, while others help us to improve this website and your experience.\n\nWe use cookies and other technologies on our website. Some of them are essential, while others help us to improve this website and your experience.\n\nPersonal data may be processed (e.g. IP addresses), for example for personalized ads and content or ad and content measurement.\n\nYou can find more information about the use of your data in our privacy policy.\n\nYou can revoke or adjust your selection at any time under Settings.\n\nThe following is a list of service groups for which consent can be given. The first service group is essential and cannot be unchecked.\nEssential\nStatistics\nExternal Media\nSave\nAccept all\nIndividual Privacy Preferences\nCookie Details\nPrivacy Policy\nImprint"}], "k": ["statistics"]}, "e0820a41ff": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Structural Engineer (m/f/x)\n\nProject management\n\nMunich\nen | de\n\nAre you looking for a new challenge and career opportunities as a civil engineer (m/f/x) at an international engineering firm in Munich? Have you successfully completed a degree in civil engineering with a focus on structural engineering? Are you eager to take on exciting professional challenges through exceptional projects in residential, industrial, and commercial construction, special structures, and building envelopes?\n\nWe are looking for a civil engineer/structural engineer (m/f/x) to start as soon as possible.\n\nYour tasks\n\nYour work will focus on developing and calculating structural designs, coordinating with the architects and specialist planners involved in the project, and effectively presenting and communicating solutions. In addition, you will take on project management responsibilities for your own projects and lead a project team independently.\n\nYour profile\n\nYou have earned a degree in civil engineering (Dipl.-Ing., M.Sc.) with a focus on structural engineering, graduating with high honors, and have at least three years of professional experience. You are open to new ideas and enjoy working in a team. You are highly motivated, a strong communicator, and work reliably and independently. You are comfortable in an international work environment and also have a good command of English.\n\nWhat Sets Us Apart\n\nWe work on innovative and unique projects both domestically and internationally—ranging from complex building structures to interdisciplinary special projects. With us, you’ll work in an international, collaborative, and interdisciplinary environment. Modern work methods such as BIM and parametric design are standard practice here."}, {"h": "We offer", "t": "A company cell phone for both work and personal use (the latest iPhone)\nMonthly reimbursement for the Deutschlandticket\nSubsidy for after-school care or daycare for children not yet of school age\nCompany pension plan\nCompany international health insurance, also for personal use\nAccident insurance\nInteresting and varied tasks in an environment of innovative and unique projects in Germany and abroad\nOpen corporate culture\nFlexible working hours\nOpportunities for exchange with other offices within the B+G Group in Germany and abroad (Erasmus program)\nInternal and external training and continuing education programs (standard: Rhino, Grasshopper, SketchUp, Revit)\nInternal interdisciplinary collaboration across structural engineering, facades, building physics, fire protection, parametric design, etc.\n“Self-directed work” and support for taking the initiative in personal development (BIM group, parametric design group, materials group, etc.)\nVarious workplace wellness initiatives\n\nHave we piqued your interest? Then send us your application—we look forward to receiving your brief application, including your resume, references, and portfolio, as well as your earliest available start date.\n\napply via applicant portal"}], "k": ["bim", "grasshopper", "parametric-design", "project-management", "revit", "rhino", "sketchup"]}, "d17bb7e694": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Structural Engineer (m/f/x)\n\nProject Work\n\nRome\nen | it\n\nTo support our team in Rome, we are looking for a structural engineer (m/f/x), preferably registered with good English skills."}, {"h": "Your duties", "t": "Structural design processing of national and international building construction projects (calculation and/or drafting)\nCoordination with architects, clients, and contractors\nDevelopment of intelligent solutions in cooperation with architects and specialist planners\nYour profile\nGood knowledge of the English language (B2/C1). Knowledge of German or French language will be considered an added value.\nGood university theoretical knowledge related to reinforced concrete and steel structures, also in a seismic zone, according to Italian standards and Eurocodes\nSpirit of analysis and synthesis, motivation, organisational skills and autonomy in one's work.\nAbility to work in an international team with good interpersonal skills\nKnowledge of the following software: Excel, Word, Finite Element Calculation Software (basic knowledge), Autocad and/or Revit and/or Rhino (basic knowledge)\nKnowledge of parametric tools (Grasshopper, Karamba, Dynamo, etc.) is a plus"}, {"h": "What we offer", "t": "Interesting and varied tasks in an environment of innovative and unique national and international projects\nPossibility to participate in an internal Erasmus programme within the B+G Group"}, {"h": "Internal and external training and further education measures", "t": "International working environment\nA motivated design team\nCollaboration with renowned architectural firms\nFlexible working hours\nCompany mobile phone after the probationary period for professional and private use\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application.\n\nInterested candidates may submit their resume to application@bollinger-grohmann.it , indicating in the subject line: Application for Structural Engineer at B+G Rome\n\nThis position is open to candidates who consent to the processing of their personal data.\n\napply via email"}], "k": ["autocad", "concrete-design", "dynamo", "excel", "grasshopper", "revit", "rhino", "steel-design", "structural-analysis"]}, "2245c35137": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Structural Engineer (m/f/x)\n\nProject manager\n\nBudapest\nen | hu"}, {"h": "About the job", "t": "Structural design for international and national projects\nConsultation with architects, builders and contractors\nDeveloping creative structural design solutions in collaboration with architects and professional designers\nManaging a team of 3-9 people"}, {"h": "Specialised qualification (M.Sc.)", "t": "Structural designer licence\nMinimum 10 years of professional experience\nIntermediate level of English and German\nGood communication skills and team spirit\nCommitment to structural design and implementation of complex structures\nAdvantages\nKnowledge of DLUBAL, MB, ETABS programs\nInternational work experience\nIntermediate knowledge of other foreign languages\nCategory B driving licence"}, {"h": "What we offer", "t": "Stable company background, long term perspective\nAbove average salary, cafeteria, mobile phone even for private use\nFull-time registered employment\nInternational experience, participation in international projects\nOpportunity to work in our foreign office on a temporary basis\nModern working tools, pleasant office environment\nFamily-friendly management, helpful colleagues, flexible working hours\nSeveral company meetings, team-builders per year\n\nIf you are interested, please send your application with your payment request to the following e-mail address. Please enclose your CV.\n\napply via email"}], "k": ["etabs", "structural-analysis"]}, "7ec1368fd9": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Climate Action\nProjects"}, {"h": "About Us", "t": "News & Insights\nContact\nSearch\nWork With Us\nAll\nLondon\nNottingham\nOxford\nBristol\nRemote Studio\n\nFrom the very first days of the practice, the focused desire to take care is a quality that has elevated our practice. We care for each other. We care for the people we collaborate with. We take care in our work and the projects we work on. And we care for our communities and for the environment.\n\nIn recent years, the practice has made a concerted effort to better reflect the diversity of the places we live and work in. We still have some way to go, but we have drawn considerable strength from the different cultures and different ways of thinking that this approach has brought us.\n\nEveryone that wants to contribute to great engineering is welcomed here. Maybe that’s you too?\n\nStructural Engineer with 3+ years' exprerience, Oxford\n\nDo you have 3+ years’ experience as a Structural Engineer? Interested in working on a broad range of projects? If so, we’d love to talk to you about what Price & Myers can offer for someone with your experience.\n\nThis is a full-time position based in our Oxford studio.\n\nPrice & Myers is committed to encouraging equality, diversity and inclusion among our workforce. We are an equal opportunity employer.\n\nNote\n\nPlease email a CV and cover letter to Ian Flewitt at careers@pricemyers.com.\n\nNo recruitment agents please.\n\nDownload\n\nDownload Full Job Specification\n\nStructural Engineer with 3-4 years' experience, Bristol\n\nWant to work with a friendly group of professionals committed to great engineering?\n\nWe are looking for an enthusiastic engineer with 3-4 years’ experience to join our newly established Bristol studio. You’ll need to: have a good, IStructE- or ICE-accredited degree in structural or civil engineering, be a good communicator, and have a desire to help us to continue designing great engineering.\n\nPrice & Myers is committed to encouraging equality, diversity and inclusion in our workforce. We are an equal opportunity employer.\n\nNote\n\nPlease send your CV and cover letter via email to Anna Wai: careers@pricemyers.com.\n\nNo recruitment agents please.\n\nDownload\n\nDownload Full Job Specification"}, {"h": "We're looking for Graduate Structural and Civil Engineers", "t": "Ready to start and grow your career in structural or civil engineering? If you're looking to commence employment as a graduate starting in Autumn/Winter 2026, we'd love to hear from you.\n\nWe are looking for sharp-minded, confident, sociable people who want to work on a variety of interesting, high-quality and challenging projects within our structural or civil engineering teams.\n\nPrice & Myers are committed to encouraging equality, diversity, and inclusion among our workforce. We are an equal opportunity employer.\n\nNote\n\nDownload the job description and email a CV and covering letter to Jamie Beeson using the following address: graduatejobs@pricemyers.com. No recruitment agents please.\n\nDownload\n\nDownload Full Job Specification\n\nSummer Placement\n\nSummer is closer than you think, so now is the time to start planning for your Summer Placement at Price & Myers. We have opportunities for sharp-minded students studying an engineering-relevant degree to join our structural or civil engineering teams.\n\nAre you an engineering undergraduate and looking for the right environment to build your CV and your portfolio? We’d love to hear from you.\n\nPrice & Myers is committed to encouraging equality, diversity and inclusion among our workforce. We are an equal opportunity employer.\n\nNote\n\nDownload the job description and email a CV and covering letter to Jamie Beeson using the following address: summerplacements@pricemyers.com\n\nNo recruitment agents please.\n\nDownload\n\nDownload Full Job Specification\n\n© Price & Myers 2026\n\nPolicies\n\nSite by Stylo"}], "k": []}}